class.description:
A [DataField] describes one value of a data file the way Godot describes typed values everywhere: a [member type], a [member hint] and a [member hint_string], like an exported property. On top of that it holds the rules of a data file: [member required], [member unique], [member allow_empty], a [member default_value], a regular expression [member pattern] and nested schemas for [Dictionary] and [Array] values.
The [member hint_string] is parsed and the [member pattern] compiled once when they are set, so validating many values costs no string splitting.
[codeblocks]
[gdscript]
var hp = DataField.new()
hp.name = &"hp"
hp.type = TYPE_INT
hp.required = true
hp.set_range(0, 100)

var rarity = DataField.new()
rarity.name = &"rarity"
rarity.set_enum_values(["common", "rare", "epic"])
[/gdscript]
[csharp]
var hp = new DataField();
hp.Name = "hp";
hp.Type = Variant.Type.Int;
hp.Required = true;
hp.SetRange(0, 100);

var rarity = new DataField();
rarity.Name = "rarity";
rarity.SetEnumValues(["common", "rare", "epic"]);
[/csharp]
[/codeblocks]
[b]Note:[/b] The property [member name] is set with [code]set_field_name()[/code]; [code skip-lint]set_name()[/code] is the setter of [member Resource.resource_name].
